      "case": "Hearsay, firsthand limits and reported cattle narrative",
      "source_ids": [
        "DCP-LETT-1819"
      ],
      "requirement": "Preserve Crump’s explicit attribution boundaries. The opening tradition is hearsay; his own knowledge begins with the 1847 journey, an officer’s report and the shown skin and horns. He says he failed to find the living herd, then switches to an account received from local people. The red-bull breeding story, seven-animal enumeration and Kennedy extermination report are therefore reported accounts at different removes, not a direct observation or measured specimen record. The separate Jerdon lagoon-cattle statement is also heard from Jerdon. Do not collapse these voices into a single Crump observation or use later Jerdon 1867 wording as contemporary Crump text.",
      "source_provenance": [
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-1819",
          "html_path": "reports/1856-1857/review/followups/blyth-crump-1819/DCP-LETT-1819.html",
          "html_sha256": "38e3c10ac0294fa0468dc4d171ae30c9ae0c325496c81ac6bf218a998563f508",
          "xml_path": "reports/1856-1857/review/followups/blyth-crump-1819/DCP-LETT-1819.xml",
          "xml_sha256": "784e6ab5029779c04cafee664325f14b347741ff454f6ffd3469659cc23be89e",
          "html_url": "https://www.darwinproject.ac.uk/letter/?docId=letters/DCP-LETT-1819.xml",
          "xml_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cambridge-collection/epsilon-data/ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06/xml/darwin-correspondence/letters/DCP-LETT-1819.xml",
          "revision": "ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06",
          "sender": "Charles Wade Crump",
          "recipient": "Edward Blyth",
          "source_reference": "DAR98:A114–A116",
          "physical_description": "Amem S 5pp with Darwin annotation",
          "transcription_in_tei": false
        }
      ],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-1819",
          "body_paragraph": 3,
          "quote": "So much I know only by hearsay— the following is of my own knowledge",
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[3]",
          "source_html_sha256": "38e3c10ac0294fa0468dc4d171ae30c9ae0c325496c81ac6bf218a998563f508"
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-1819",
          "body_paragraph": 4,
          "quote": "went out after this herd but could not find them, however they were perfectly well known to all the people thereabouts and the account I received was as follows—",
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[4]",
          "source_html_sha256": "38e3c10ac0294fa0468dc4d171ae30c9ae0c325496c81ac6bf218a998563f508"
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-1819",
          "body_paragraph": 5,
          "quote": "wild cattle were 7 in number",
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[5]",
          "source_html_sha256": "38e3c10ac0294fa0468dc4d171ae30c9ae0c325496c81ac6bf218a998563f508"
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-1819",
          "body_paragraph": 6,
          "quote": "I heard afterwards that the whole race was exterminated by Kennedy",
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[6]",
          "source_html_sha256": "38e3c10ac0294fa0468dc4d171ae30c9ae0c325496c81ac6bf218a998563f508"
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-1819",
          "body_paragraph": 7,
          "quote": "I have heard from Jerden of another breed of wild cattle living in the salt water lagoons and islands above Nellore",
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[7]",
          "source_html_sha256": "38e3c10ac0294fa0468dc4d171ae30c9ae0c325496c81ac6bf218a998563f508"
        }
      ]
